## 3. L2 invariants — deferred, named, not orphaned

Each is undecidable in JSON Schema (`design.md` §2.3). Fixture ids are **reserved** so the corpus
can grow into them without renumbering.

| Invariant | Rule | Why L1 can't | Successor goal | Reserved fixtures |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `INV-ID-1` | `kind` == `id`'s middle segment | cross-field string compare | F-INVARIANTS | `I30` |
| `INV-HASH-1` | `content_hash` == `sha256(JCS(content))` | requires hashing | F-INVARIANTS | `I31` |
| `INV-TIME-1` | `updated_at >= created_at`; `promotion.at >= created_at`; `confidence.computed_at >= created_at` | value comparison | F-INVARIANTS | `I32`-`I34` |
| `INV-EV-2` | `promotion.evidence_refs ⊆ evidence_refs` | subset of a sibling array | F-INVARIANTS | `I35` |
| `INV-LIN-1` | every `derived_from` resolves; lineage is acyclic | cross-document | F-INVARIANTS | `I36` |
| `INV-REF-1` | `superseded_by` / `retraction.successor` / `deprecation.prefer_instead` resolve | cross-document | F-INVARIANTS | `I37` |
| `INV-REF-2` | every `evidence_ref` resolves to an existing, non-`RETRACTED` evidence node | cross-document | F-INVARIANTS | `I38` |
| `INV-SEQ-1` | the stored transition *history* is a legal path (L1 checks one hop; a path needs the log) | cross-document | F-STORE | `I39` |
| `INV-DUP-1` | two `ACTIVE` nodes may not share a `content_hash` | cross-document | F-DEDUP | `I40` |
| `INV-CONF-6` | `value` is the number `method` would actually produce from `inputs` | requires the confidence engine | F-CONFIDENCE | `I41` |

`INV-CONF-6` is the most important deferral and should be stated plainly: **L1 proves a confidence
was derived, not that it was derived correctly.** The schema makes authoring structurally
impossible; it does not make lying arithmetically impossible. That is F-CONFIDENCE's job, and
`CANARY-0001`'s "re-run and compare" mechanism (`constitution/canaries/CANARY-0001.json:6`) is the
model for how it should work.

